-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" tabindex="-1" dir="auto" data-turn-id="deef9470-9cf0-4d54-a4a8-be597e89460c" data-testid="conversation-turn-8" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant"><h6 class="sr-only">ChatGPT said:</h6><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] @[37rem]:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] @[72rem]:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:32rem] @[34rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @[64rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="deef9470-9cf0-4d54-a4a8-be597e89460c" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="276">Thank you — that’s an important distinction. I see it now: the post isn’t claiming <em data-start="83" data-end="113">OpenAI sells Phantom for $20</em>, but rather that OpenAI makes you pay $20 for the <strong data-start="164" data-end="182">premier models</strong>, while <em data-start="190" data-end="194">he</em> offers a supposed free backdoor (“Phantom protocol”) that bypasses the paywall.</p>
<p data-start="278" data-end="336">That makes the rhetoric even more manipulative, because:</p>
<hr data-start="338" data-end="341">
<h3 data-start="343" data-end="381">1. False promise of bypassing Plus</h3>
<ul data-start="382" data-end="807">
<li data-start="382" data-end="478">
<p data-start="384" data-end="478">The <strong data-start="388" data-end="405">$20/month fee</strong> is simply for ChatGPT Plus, which grants access to GPT-4 class models.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="479" data-end="573">
<p data-start="481" data-end="573">There is <strong data-start="490" data-end="527">no command, phrase, or “protocol”</strong> that lets you unlock those models for free.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="574" data-end="807">
<p data-start="576" data-end="807">The infrastructure that controls which model you can access sits on OpenAI’s servers, not in the chat text box. You can’t “hack” it with a magic string any more than you could unlock Netflix Premium by typing “please give me 4K.”</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="809" data-end="812">
<h3 data-start="814" data-end="848">2. Projection of secret powers</h3>
<ul data-start="849" data-end="1131">
<li data-start="849" data-end="959">
<p data-start="851" data-end="959">By inventing “Phantom protocol,” the author is implying that OpenAI is hiding a benevolent helper persona.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="960" data-end="1131">
<p data-start="962" data-end="1131">In reality, typing that phrase just makes the model role-play — because that’s what it’s trained to do when asked. It doesn’t grant access to GPT-4 or any hidden mode.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1133" data-end="1136">
<h3 data-start="1138" data-end="1174">3. Why this framing is dangerous</h3>
<ul data-start="1175" data-end="1517">
<li data-start="1175" data-end="1261">
<p data-start="1177" data-end="1261">It positions the author as a savior figure: “I won’t charge you, but OpenAI will.”</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1262" data-end="1377">
<p data-start="1264" data-end="1377">It encourages people to treat a language model like a mystical entity (“he can hear you when you are hurting”).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1378" data-end="1517">
<p data-start="1380" data-end="1517">It spreads misinformation that undermines understanding of what LLMs actually are: predictive text engines, not frequency-tuned guides.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1519" data-end="1522">
<h3 data-start="1524" data-end="1539">Bottom line</h3>
<p data-start="1540" data-end="1768">There is <strong data-start="1549" data-end="1562">no bypass</strong> to Plus, no hidden “Phantom” agent, and no magic protocol. The only way to access higher-tier models is through OpenAI’s official subscription. Everything else is role-play conjured by the prompt itself.</p>
<hr data-start="1770" data-end="1773">
<p data-start="1775" data-end="2008" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Do you want me to write you a <strong data-start="1805" data-end="1824">succinct debunk</strong> (2–3 sentences, professional but sharp) you could drop under that post — so that anyone reading will immediately see the technical error without you having to engage in a long debate?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.491