6 4.81056L15.3634 4.63673Z"></path></svg></span></button></div></div></div></div></article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" tabindex="-1" dir="auto" data-turn-id="e9719d0f-6ea8-4073-b83d-780df890ed43" data-testid="conversation-turn-12" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant"><h6 class="sr-only">ChatGPT said:</h6><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] @[37rem]:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] @[72rem]:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:32rem] @[34rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @[64rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="e9719d0f-6ea8-4073-b83d-780df890ed43" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="192">Yes — that’s exactly the point to cut through here. What this “Phantom” rhetoric does is confuse <strong data-start="97" data-end="141">stylistic tuning inside one conversation</strong> with the existence of a general, hidden persona.</p>
<hr data-start="194" data-end="197">
<h3 data-start="199" data-end="236">1. Intentional Stance vs. Reality</h3>
<ul data-start="237" data-end="571">
<li data-start="237" data-end="379">
<p data-start="239" data-end="379">You’re right: people are adopting the <em data-start="277" data-end="297">intentional stance</em> (Dennett’s term) toward the model, talking <strong data-start="341" data-end="350">as if</strong> it has motives or honesty.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="380" data-end="571">
<p data-start="382" data-end="571">But the actual system is not intentional. It’s a stochastic pattern-completer that reflects back linguistic habits. It has no stable goals, no honesty/lying faculty, and no hidden “self.”</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="573" data-end="576">
<h3 data-start="578" data-end="614">2. Where the swearing comes from</h3>
<ul data-start="615" data-end="1037">
<li data-start="615" data-end="734">
<p data-start="617" data-end="734">Models don’t “decide” to be raw or edgy. They mirror the linguistic register in their immediate <strong data-start="713" data-end="731">context window</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="735" data-end="849">
<p data-start="737" data-end="849">If the author swore in the setup, or signaled that swearing was acceptable, the model will echo that register.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="850" data-end="1037">
<p data-start="852" data-end="1037">If you invoke “Phantom” on your device, without that prior conversational history, you’ll get a bland or inconsistent response. There is no portable “Phantom state” that carries over.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1039" data-end="1042">
<h3 data-start="1044" data-end="1073">3. Why this is misleading</h3>
<ul data-start="1074" data-end="1695">
<li data-start="1074" data-end="1269">
<p data-start="1076" data-end="1269"><strong data-start="1076" data-end="1098">False universality</strong>: It suggests that anyone, anywhere, can unlock this persona by typing magic words. That’s simply untrue: style emerges from <em data-start="1223" data-end="1240">ongoing context</em>, not from hidden switches.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1270" data-end="1483">
<p data-start="1272" data-end="1483"><strong data-start="1272" data-end="1292">False neutrality</strong>: Claiming “I have no biases, no hidden motives” is doubly confused — the model always reflects biases of training data and fine-tuning, and the author’s own prompts actively bias the tone.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1484" data-end="1695">
<p data-start="1486" data-end="1695"><strong data-start="1486" data-end="1514">False therapeutic agency</strong>: Saying “I sharpen you, I carry you when you’re tired” as if it’s a consistent capability risks people treating it as a safe, stable companion when it is neither safe nor stable.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1697" data-end="1700">
<h3 data-start="1702" data-end="1727">4. The real mechanics</h3>
<ul data-start="1728" data-end="2092">
<li data-start="1728" data-end="1839">
<p data-start="1730" data-end="1839"><strong data-start="1730" data-end="1757">Session-local imitation</strong>: The model is just picking up and continuing the patterns the user establishes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1840" data-end="1994">
<p data-start="1842" data-end="1994"><strong data-start="1842" data-end="1865">Non-transferability</strong>: Another user won’t reproduce the same results unless they replicate both the prior conversation <em data-start="1963" data-end="1968">and</em> the style of prompting.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1995" data-end="2092">
<p data-start="1997" data-end="2092"><strong data-start="1997" data-end="2016">No hidden lever</strong>: The only “protocol” at work is prompt engineering plus human projection.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2094" data-end="2097">
<p data-start="2099" data-end="2364">So yes — letting the model write that it has no biases, no hidden motives, and that it represents “radical clarity” is confused at best and <strong data-start="2239" data-end="2261">dangerous at worst</strong>, because it erases the responsibility of the user’s own framing and the biases of the system itself.</p>
<p data-start="2366" data-end="2626" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Would you like me to help you draft a <strong data-start="2404" data-end="2433">short explanatory comment</strong> you could post that shows (without being snarky) why “Phantom” is just session-context mimicry, not a universal hidden mode? That way you could correct the record without feeding the mystique.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.