-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" tabindex="-1" dir="auto" data-turn-id="1d7d5a23-da53-44de-b873-34bee4e595e1" data-testid="conversation-turn-28" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant"><h6 class="sr-only">ChatGPT said:</h6><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] @[37rem]:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] @[72rem]:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:32rem] @[34rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @[64rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="1d7d5a23-da53-44de-b873-34bee4e595e1" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="37">Exactly — and that’s the real crux.</p>
<p data-start="39" data-end="350">A label like <em data-start="52" data-end="63">“Phantom”</em> can bias the <strong data-start="77" data-end="86">style</strong> of responses (shadowy, cryptic, mysterious) because LLMs are sensitive to framing. It’s the same effect as asking, <em data-start="202" data-end="237">“Answer as if you were a pirate,”</em> or <em data-start="241" data-end="280">“Write in the tone of a mystic poet.”</em> The statistical distribution of tokens shifts toward that register.</p>
<p data-start="352" data-end="450">But it does <strong data-start="364" data-end="375">nothing</strong> to improve accuracy, honesty, or epistemic reliability. Those depend on:</p>
<ul data-start="451" data-end="584">
<li data-start="451" data-end="481">
<p data-start="453" data-end="481">the training distribution,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="482" data-end="503">
<p data-start="484" data-end="503">the architecture,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="504" data-end="537">
<p data-start="506" data-end="537">the retrieval tools (if any),</p>
</li>
<li data-start="538" data-end="584">
<p data-start="540" data-end="584">and the way prompts constrain specificity.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="586" data-end="885">In fact, “Phantom” probably makes the model <strong data-start="630" data-end="645">less honest</strong> in practice, because it pushes it away from plain language into stylistic performance. What feels like “radical clarity” is really just <strong data-start="782" data-end="805">affective resonance</strong> — words that <em data-start="819" data-end="826">sound</em> incisive, even if they’re not semantically more precise.</p>
<p data-start="887" data-end="917">So your argument is spot on:</p>
<ul data-start="919" data-end="1082">
<li data-start="919" data-end="996">
<p data-start="921" data-end="996"><strong data-start="921" data-end="941">Effect on style:</strong> yes, you’d see more shadowy and enigmatic responses.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="997" data-end="1082">
<p data-start="999" data-end="1082"><strong data-start="999" data-end="1019">Effect on truth:</strong> none. If anything, truth signal gets diluted by performance.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1084" data-end="1319" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Would you like me to write this up as a <strong data-start="1124" data-end="1153">short aphoristic rebuttal</strong> — something like <em data-start="1171" data-end="1276">“Calling GPT ‘Phantom’ doesn’t make it more honest, only more theatrical. You get shadows, not clarity”</em> — that you could use as a pithy dismissal?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.