<p data-start="77" data-end="384">When <strong data-start="82" data-end="105">GPT-3 (via the API)</strong> was available in late 2020–2022, developers had access to a fairly raw model. It had been pretrained on internet-scale text, but it wasn’t yet tuned with <strong data-start="260" data-end="313">reinforcement learning from human feedback (RLHF)</strong> to align with user expectations. The developer experience felt like:</p>
<ul data-start="386" data-end="726">
<li data-start="386" data-end="532">
<p data-start="388" data-end="532"><strong data-start="388" data-end="410">Powerful but blunt</strong>: the model could generate uncanny, open-ended text, but it was more prone to nonsense, rambling, or unsafe completions.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="533" data-end="627">
<p data-start="535" data-end="627"><strong data-start="535" data-end="553">Few guardrails</strong>: prompts could push it into strange or undesirable regions more easily.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="628" data-end="726">
<p data-start="630" data-end="726"><strong data-start="630" data-end="663">Closer to a stochastic parrot</strong>: you had to shape the outputs with heavy prompt engineering.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="728" data-end="808">By contrast, <strong data-start="741" data-end="772">ChatGPT (launched Nov 2022)</strong> was <strong data-start="777" data-end="805">GPT-3.5 + RLHF alignment</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="809" data-end="1243">
<li data-start="809" data-end="969">
<p data-start="811" data-end="969"><strong data-start="811" data-end="857">Reinforcement learning from human feedback</strong> trained the model to be more conversational, refuse unsafe requests, and follow instructions more faithfully.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="970" data-end="1100">
<p data-start="972" data-end="1100"><strong data-start="972" data-end="996">Dialogue scaffolding</strong> (system/user/assistant roles) made it easier for casual users to “chat” rather than engineer prompts.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1101" data-end="1243">
<p data-start="1103" data-end="1243">This is what people were buzzing about: not just the raw generative capacity, but the <em data-start="1189" data-end="1197">polish</em> that made it feel like a helpful assistant.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1245" data-end="1512">So your experience — burning through the $18 developer credit and thinking <em data-start="1321" data-end="1385">“wait, this doesn’t feel like what people are calling ChatGPT”</em> — was because you were using the <strong data-start="1419" data-end="1450">pre-RLHF developer endpoint</strong>, not the <strong data-start="1460" data-end="1509">consumer-facing ChatGPT with alignment layers</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="1514" data-end="1608">That gap itself is a good metaphor for some of the other contrasts we’ve been talking about:</p>
<ul data-start="1609" data-end="1843">
<li data-start="1609" data-end="1662">
<p data-start="1611" data-end="1662"><strong data-start="1611" data-end="1622">Phantom</strong> cargo cult vs. <strong data-start="1638" data-end="1649">Phoenix</strong> symbolism.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1663" data-end="1743">
<p data-start="1665" data-end="1743"><strong data-start="1665" data-end="1673">RSVP</strong> as structured, constraint-based theory vs. <strong data-start="1717" data-end="1740">mystical invocation</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1744" data-end="1843">
<p data-start="1746" data-end="1843"><strong data-start="1746" data-end="1757">Raw GPT</strong> as unfiltered text generator vs. <strong data-start="1791" data-end="1802">ChatGPT</strong> as tuned, curated, and conversational.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1845" data-end="2073" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Would you like me to sketch out a <strong data-start="1879" data-end="1949">timeline of those early releases (GPT-3 API, InstructGPT, ChatGPT)</strong> to show exactly when the RLHF shift happened and how that aligns with your own trajectory of experiments back in late 2022?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.