<p data-start="4559" data-end="4583"><strong data-start="4559" data-end="4581">Style constraints.</strong></p>
<ul data-start="4584" data-end="4838">
<li data-start="4584" data-end="4656">
<p data-start="4586" data-end="4656">Prefer theorems/lemmas/scaling claims with short proofs or sketches.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4657" data-end="4700">
<p data-start="4659" data-end="4700">Use counterexamples where hype appears.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4701" data-end="4776">
<p data-start="4703" data-end="4776">Explicitly separate <strong data-start="4723" data-end="4736">stylistic</strong> prompts from <strong data-start="4750" data-end="4765">mechanistic</strong> effects.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4777" data-end="4838">
<p data-start="4779" data-end="4838">When unsure, state bounds and assumptions, not certainties.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="4840" data-end="5243"><strong data-start="4840" data-end="4873">Example (one‑liner template).</strong><br data-start="4873" data-end="4876">
“Given <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span></span></span></span>, let <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Φ</span></span></span></span> denote capacity, <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4444em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span></span></span></span> the propagation field, and <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span></span> the uncertainty. Under <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">∂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</m