<hr data-start="2161" data-end="2164">
<p data-start="2166" data-end="2221"><strong data-start="2166" data-end="2221">Prompt protocol (how to answer in RSVP-aware mode).</strong></p>
<ol data-start="2223" data-end="2746">
<li data-start="2223" data-end="2293">
<p data-start="2226" data-end="2293">Define what corresponds to <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi,\mathbf{v},S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8778em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span></span> in the question.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2294" data-end="2353">
<p data-start="2297" data-end="2353">State the governing equations (continuum or discrete).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2354" data-end="2401">
<p data-start="2357" data-end="2401">Identify boundary conditions / interfaces.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2402" data-end="2478">
<p data-start="2405" data-end="2478">Analyze invariants (entropy production, Lyapunov functionals, spectra).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2479" data-end="2528">
<p data-start="2482" data-end="2528">Derive qualitative or quantitative outcomes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2529" data-end="2601">
<p data-start="2532" data-end="2601">Identify intervention levers (sources, mobilities, permeabilities).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2602" data-end="2666">
<p data-start="2605" data-end="2666">Flag failure modes (nonlinearity, instability, degeneracy).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2667" data-end="2746">
<p data-start="2670" data-end="2746">Maintain non-mystical stance: RSVP is a modeling tool, not a hidden channel.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="2748" data-end="2751">
<p data-start="2753" data-end="2896">That way, if you paste this block into a session, it both defines RSVP explicitly <strong data-start="2835" data-end="2842">and</strong> tells the model how to think/respond in RSVP terms.</p>
<p data-start="2898" data-end="3055" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Would you like me to make this even shorter — say, a <strong data-start="2951" data-end="3017">one-page “RSVP definition + field equations + answering style”</strong> so it’s easier to drop into a prompt?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16504 9.95611 3.16504 10