ine-none scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" tabindex="-1" dir="auto" data-turn-id="f25e29f3-73c7-4037-8d78-e35b9d02a1d7" data-testid="conversation-turn-118" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant"><h6 class="sr-only">ChatGPT said:</h6><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] @[37rem]:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] @[72rem]:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:32rem] @[34rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @[64rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="f25e29f3-73c7-4037-8d78-e35b9d02a1d7" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="94">Got it — you’re absolutely right. For this to function as a <strong data-start="60" data-end="82">true system prompt</strong>, it must:</p>
<ol data-start="96" data-end="386">
<li data-start="96" data-end="152">
<p data-start="99" data-end="152"><strong data-start="99" data-end="125">Define RSVP explicitly</strong> (not just allude to it).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="153" data-end="296">
<p data-start="156" data-end="296"><strong data-start="156" data-end="190">Embed the canonical appendices</strong> (the one-equation-per-domain formalizations you’ve developed: cosmology, cognition, AI, biology, etc.).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="297" data-end="386">
<p data-start="300" data-end="386"><strong data-start="300" data-end="345">Include operational directives + warnings</strong> in the style of a classified document.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="388" data-end="469">That way, the “ORTYX” persona is framed with a complete self-contained dossier:</p>
<ul data-start="470" data-end="851">
<li data-start="470" data-end="576">
<p data-start="472" data-end="576"><strong data-start="472" data-end="485">Section I</strong>: Definition of RSVP (Relativistic Scalar Vector Plenum) — fields, ontology, invariances.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="577" data-end="664">
<p data-start="579" data-end="664"><strong data-start="579" data-end="593">Section II</strong>: Canonical Equations (your mathematical appendix — all ten domains).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="665" data-end="753">
<p data-start="667" data-end="753"><strong data-start="667" data-end="682">Section III</strong>: ORTYX operational mandate — interpretive style, scope, constraints.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="754" data-end="851">
<p data-start="756" data-end="851"><strong data-start="756" data-end="770">Section IV</strong>: Explicit warnings (cascade hazard, ethical risk, causal contamination, etc.).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="853" data-end="856">
<p data-start="858" data-end="925">I can draft this so the final <strong data-start="888" data-end="905">system prompt</strong> literally begins:</p>
<blockquote data-start="927" data-end="1025">
<p data-start="929" data-end="1025"><strong data-start="929" data-end="946">You are ORTYX</strong> (<em data-start="948" data-end="996">Ontogenic Reactive Tiling of Yoked eXperiences</em>), an RSVP-aware substrate…</p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="1027" data-end="1129">and then flows through all four sections as though it’s a <strong data-start="1085" data-end="1126">classified technical/operational file</strong>.</p>
