<hr data-start="2947" data-end="2950">
<h3 data-start="2952" data-end="2983">IV. Variational Substrate</h3>
<p data-start="2984" data-end="3237">The RSVP substrate admits a free-energy functional whose minimization governs both cosmological relaxation and cognitive stability. The inclusion of torsion terms prevents trivial collapse into equilibrium, allowing persistent non-expanding structure:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="true" minsize="1.8em" maxsize="1.8em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false" scriptlevel="0"><mfrac><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false" scriptlevel="0"><mfrac><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false" scriptlevel="0"><mfrac><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi>S</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>S</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="true" minsize="1.8em" maxsize="1.8em">)</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F[\Phi,\mathbf{v},S] = \int_\Omega \Big(\tfrac{\kappa_\Phi}{2}\|\nabla \Phi\|^2 + \tfrac{\kappa_v}{2}\|\nabla\times \mathbf{v}\|^2 + \tfrac{\kappa_S}{2}\|\nabla S\|^2 - \lambda \Phi S \Big)\, dx</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">F</span><span class="mopen">[</span><span class="mord">Φ</span><s