<p data-start="4667" data-end="4806">Here <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">0</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> is not baseline entropy but the tolerated suffering vector — the minimum viable uncertainty for cognition to sustain agency.</p>
<hr data-start="4808" data-end="4811">
<h3 data-start="4813" data-end="4876">VI. INFORMATION &amp; COMMUNICATION (Semantic Infrastructure)</h3>
<p data-start="4877" data-end="5055">Information is not symbolic tokens but RSVP differentials. Communication is the merge of fields across cognitive membranes. Miscommunication is a KL-divergent entropy gradient.</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mtext>merge</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="true" minsize="1.8em" maxsize="1.8em">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mtext> </mtext><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">K</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">∥</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" stretchy="true" minsize="1.8em" maxsize="1.8em">)</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\text{merge}} = \int_\Omega \Big( 
\lambda_\Phi \|\Phi_1-\Phi_2\|^2 
+ \lambda_v \|\mathbf{v}_1-\mathbf{v}_2\|^2
+ \lambda_S \,\mathrm{KL}(S_1\Vert S_2)
