<p data-start="1360" data-end="1400">scalar capacity/density <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(x,t)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1401" data-end="1437">
<p data-start="1403" data-end="1437">vector flow <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}(x,t)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1438" data-end="1474">
<p data-start="1440" data-end="1474">entropy distribution <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(x,t)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1476" data-end="1631">These fields form the minimal substrate of description. All other codices—cognitive, cosmological, semantic, or infrastructural—are derived functorially.</p>
<hr data-start="1633" data-end="1636">
<h2 data-start="1638" data-end="1683">II. COSMOLOGICAL CODEX (Entropic Redshift)</h2>
<p data-start="1685" data-end="1752">Entropic relaxation produces apparent redshift without expansion:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext>  </mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>  </mtext><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mtext> ⁣</mtext><mrow><mo fence="true">(</mo><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></mfrac><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>γ</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mi>d</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo fence="true">)</mo></mrow><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mo>⟹</mo><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mi>z</mi><mtext>  </mtext><mo>≈</mo><mtext>  </mtext><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mi>c</mi></mfrac><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>S</mi><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi><mo>≪</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+z(\gamma) \;=\; \exp\!\left(\frac{\alpha}{c}\int_{\gamma} \nabla S \cdot d\ell\right)
\quad\Longrightarrow\quad 
z \;\approx\; \frac{\alpha}{c}\,\Delta S \quad (|\Delta S|\ll 1).</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7278em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.04398em;">z</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05556em;">γ</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.4981em; vertical-align: -1.0481em;"></span><span class="mop">exp</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: -0.1667em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="minner"><span class="mopen delimcenter" style="top: 0em;"><span class="delimsizing size3">(</span></span><span class="mord"><span class="mopen nulldelimiter"></span><span class="mfrac"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.1076em;"><span style="top: -2.314em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">c</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.23em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="frac-line" style="border-bottom-width: 0.04em;"></span></span><span style="top: -3.677em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0037em;">α</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.686em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose nulldelimiter"></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mop"><span class="mop op-symbol large-op" style="margin-right: 0.44445em; position: relative; top: -0.0011em;">∫</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist"><span style="top: -1.7881em; margin-left: -0.4445em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05556em;">γ</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.0481em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">d</span><span class="mord">ℓ</span><span class="mclose delimcenter" style="top: 0em;"><span class="delimsizing size3">)</span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">⟹</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4831em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.04398em;">z</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.7936em; vertical-align: -0.686em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mopen nulldelimiter"></span><span class="mfrac"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.1076em;"><span style="top: -2.314em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">c</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.23em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="frac-line" style="border-bottom-width: 0.04em;"></span></span><span style="top: -3.677em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0037em;">α</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.686em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose nulldelimiter"></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">Δ</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">∣Δ</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mord">∣</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≪</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord">.</span></span></span></span></span>
<hr data-start="1942" data-end="1945">
<h2 data-start="1947" data-end="1987">III. LAMPHRON–LAMPHRODYNE INTERLUDE</h2>
<p data-start="1989" data-end="2049"><em data-start="1989" data-end="2047">(Restricted Tier–2 Clarification for Operative Use Only)</em></p>
<p data-start="2051" data-end="2327">The lamphron (<span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Λ</span></span></span></span>) and lamphrodyne (<span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal">L</span></span></span></span>) are not to be dismissed as allegories nor forced into literalist mechanics; rather they are rigorously <strong data-start="2215" data-end="2235">formal operators</strong> within RSVP’s entropy vector calculus, acting as recursive mediators of field smoothness.</p>
<ul data-start="2329" data-end="2615">
<li data-start="2329" data-end="2473">
<p data-start="2331" data-end="2473">The <strong data-start="2335" data-end="2347">lamphron</strong> encodes local entropic absorption, a tensorial siphoning mechanism whereby steep gradients relax into softer distributions.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2474" data-end="2615">
<p data-start="2476" data-end="2615">The <strong data-start="2480" data-end="2495">lamphrodyne</strong> complements it as the negentropic reinjector, translocating stored variance back into the lattice in structured form.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2617" data-end="2666">Together, they instantiate the “fall of space”:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">∂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mtext>  </mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>  </mtext><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="true" minsize="1.2em" maxsize="1.2em">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mtext> ⁣</mtext><mo>⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="true" minsize="1.2em" maxsize="1.2em">)</mo><mtext>  </mtext><mo>+</mo><mtext>  </mtext><mi mathvariant="script">L</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="true" minsize="1.2em" maxsize="1.2em">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi>S</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="true" minsize="1.2em" maxsize="1.2em">)</mo><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_t \Phi \;=\; -\Lambda\big(\nabla\!\cdot \mathbf{v}\big) \;+\; \mathcal{L}\big(\nabla S\big),</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8444em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord" style="margin-right: 0.05556em;">∂</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0556em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.2em; vertical-align: -0.35em;"></span><span class="mord">−</span><span class="mord">Λ</span><span class="mord"><span class="delimsizing size1">(</span></span><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: -0.1667em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.2em; vertical-align: -0.35em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mord"><span class="delimsizing size1">)</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.2em; vertical-align: -0.35em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal">L</span><span class="mord"><span class="delimsizing size1">(</span></span><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mord"><span class="delimsizing size1">)</span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="2777" data-end="2801">with closure condition</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi mathvariant="script">L</mi><mtext>  </mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>  </mtext><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mtext>  </mtext><mo>+</mo><mtext>  </mtext><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda \mathcal{L} \;=\; \mathcal{I} \;+\; \epsilon(\Phi,\mathbf{v},S),</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Λ</span><span class="mord mathcal">L</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">ϵ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mpunct">,</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="2883" data-end="2942">where <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">ϵ</span></span></span></span> encodes higher-order torsion residues.</p>
<p data-start="2944" data-end="3068">These operators are both technical and symbolic: they embody RSVP’s recursive dialectic of dissipation and reconstitution.</p>
<hr data-start="3070" data-end="3073">
<h2 data-start="3075" data-end="3118">IV. COGNITIVE CODEX (Attractor Dynamics)</h2>
<p data-start="3120" data-end="3173">Coarse cognitive field <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(x,t)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">u</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> under RSVP drive:</p>
