 class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">T</span></span></span></span>. There is a natural transformation <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="bold">C</mi><mi mathvariant="bold">o</mi><mi mathvariant="bold">m</mi><mi mathvariant="bold">p</mi></mrow><mo>⇒</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="bold">C</mi><mi mathvariant="bold">o</mi><mi mathvariant="bold">u</mi><mi mathvariant="bold">n</mi><mi mathvariant="bold">t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N:\mathbf{Comp}\Rightarrow\mathbf{Count}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">N</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8805em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbf">Comp</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">⇒</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbf">Count</span></span></span></span></span> such that <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>⪰</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta S\succeq (\ln 2)\,N</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span clas